# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces current production (#4522): the
# committed-values backstop installs a key the terminal finds no bucket for at
# a freshly ticked stamp, above whatever the row holds, instead of
# last-writer-wins at the saga's own prepare stamp. A terminal that reaches a
# split destination after a later write of the moved key has landed there
# overwrites that acknowledged write. The edit lies in TermRow, the operator
# the terminal broadcast applies, so the mutation declares no PERTURBS.
MODULE: NoKeyLostFreshStampBackstop
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the terminal's backstop installs over a later write with a dominating stamp

--- FIND
    ELSE IF pend[c][s][k] = "old" \/ MapOf(CopyMap(c), k) = s THEN Max(row[c][s][k], SagaV)
--- REPLACE
    ELSE IF pend[c][s][k] = "old" THEN Max(row[c][s][k], SagaV)
\* MUTATION: the backstop is stamped above the row, whatever the row holds.
    ELSE IF MapOf(CopyMap(c), k) = s THEN SagaV
--- END
